From 186fc521f211a207c323b753659f28d3dda7bc45 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 12:46:22 +0200
Subject: backlight: qcom-wled: Fix NULL pointer dereference in wled_remove()
Git-commit: 186fc521f211a207c323b753659f28d3dda7bc45
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc1
References: git-fixes

wled_probe() doesn't set the driver data for the platform device.
As a result, platform_get_drvdata() in wled_remove() will return NULL,
and the first dereference of it crashes on unbind.

Set the platform device driver data in wled_probe().

Cc: stable@vger.kernel.org
Fixes: feeab87b3072 ("backlight: qcom-wled: Add support for short circuit handling")
Signed-off-by: David Heidelberg <david@ixit.cz>
Reviewed-by: Daniel Thompson (RISCstar) <danielt@kernel.org>
Reviewed-by: Konrad Dybcio <konrad.dybcio@oss.qualcomm.com>
Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260921-qcom-wled-backlight-v4-1-bab8c7ef73cb@ixit.cz
Signed-off-by: Lee Jones <lee@kernel.org>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c b/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
index 650dd95f06ef..2281007bdd45 100644
--- a/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
+++ b/drivers/video/backlight/qcom-wled.c
@@ -1680,6 +1680,7 @@ static int wled_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 	wled->regmap = regmap;
 	wled->dev = &pdev->dev;
+	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, wled);
 
 	wled->version = (uintptr_t)of_device_get_match_data(&pdev->dev);
 	if (!wled->version) {
-- 
